      en: "Côn Đảo National Park is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Vietnam. A national park comprising an archipelago of 16 islands off the coast of southern Vietnam. It protects both terrestrial and marine ecosystems, including coral reefs and sea turtle nesting sites. Major nesting site for Green and Hawksbill turtles. Includes pristine beaches and coral reefs. Home to dugongs (sea cows). This natural area reflects the scenic diversity of Vietnam, from Ha Long Bay to the iconic rice terraces. Like many notable places in Vietnam, it combines regional character with the legacy of a millennia-old civilization and the French colonial era. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Vietnam — from the Mekong Delta and Ha Long Bay to the terraced rice fields.",
